Z||000003||Eric||01-30-2000||03:23 PM||||I'd like to build a 427 Cobra replica.  The kit I'm looking at is made by Factory Five and uses a donor 5.0 for the engine and rear end and a few other parts.  According to them, it outperforms an original 427 because of the weight savings (tips the scales at 2,000lbs).  From the looks of it, the kit appears to be a real 427 from the outside.  For 15-20k you can't beat it.  Think of all the heads it would turn.  Anyway, if there are any 5.0 guys out there in Fiero World, I would like to get some advice on engine buildups to generate around 400-450hp (right now I know very little about 5.0s).  Do Mustangs count as little cars with big engines?  I don't want to venture too far off the thread topic. ||||reg||7
